---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout lang="en" title="Workshop Stage Fencing & Fight Choreography — Ilian Simeonow"  description="Stage fencing and fight choreography workshop with Ilian Simeonow. For actors, sport fencers and beginners." heroImage="/images/stunt/Fechten-2.jpg">

  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="hero-top-bar"></div>
    <div class="page-hero-content">
      <div class="section-label">// Workshop · 01</div>
      <h1 class="page-hero-title">Workshop<br /><span style="color: var(--orange);">Stage Fencing</span></h1>
      <p class="page-hero-sub">Stage Fencing · Fight Choreography · Stage Combat</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="article-section">
    <div class="article-grid">
      <div class="article-body">
        <p class="article-intro">
          Stage fencing has long been a core part of drama school training — and for good reason. Ilian Simeonow teaches fencing as a performative art: technically precise, scenically convincing, and safe for everyone involved.
        </p>

        <h2 class="article-h2">What This Workshop Develops</h2>
        <p>Alongside the obvious advantages at castings for relevant productions, stage fencing training builds the following qualities:</p>
        <ul class="article-list">
          <li><strong>Concentration</strong> — precision in the moment, focus on your partner</li>
          <li><strong>Fitness & Endurance</strong> — fencing is physically demanding</li>
          <li><strong>Inner Calm & Confidence</strong> — control under pressure</li>
          <li><strong>Responsibility for Your Partner</strong> — safety as a shared goal</li>
          <li><strong>Precision</strong> — exact execution of every movement</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Fencing is also an excellent way to build general health, fitness and athleticism.</p>

        <h2 class="article-h2">Who Is This Workshop For?</h2>
        <p>This workshop is open to sport fencers, interested laypersons and actors alike. Brave beginners are also very welcome — you will learn something regardless of your level.</p>
        <p>The training content is similar to a beginner fencing workshop but at a higher level, with the emphasis on tactics and their application in stage combat.</p>
        <p>Renaissance weapon combinations such as rapier and dagger or cloak and rapier are historically central — the workshop focuses on the rapier as the primary weapon. Single- or two-handed weapons and combinations such as shield and axe or lance are also possible on request.</p>

        <h2 class="article-h2">What Will You Learn?</h2>
        <p>Key elements of the course:</p>
        <ul class="article-list">
          <li><strong>Physical Conditioning</strong> — general and fencing-specific</li>
          <li><strong>Strength & Endurance</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Reaction & Stretching</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Technique & Tactics</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Footwork</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Partner Exercises</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Attack & Defence Techniques</strong> — culminating in a short staged choreography</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="article-h2">What to Bring</h2>
        <ul class="article-list">
          <li>Comfortable sportswear</li>
          <li>Indoor sports shoes</li>
          <li>Gloves</li>
          <li>Good mood</li>
        </ul>
        <p>No prior experience in stage combat is required. Weapons are provided — but feel free to bring your own.</p>

        <div class="article-callout">
          <div class="section-label">// Pricing & Booking</div>
          <p>All prices plus VAT and travel costs (€0.30/km). Also suitable for larger groups. Ilian comes to you or you come to him.</p>
          <a href="/en/contact/" class="link-more">Request a non-binding offer →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="article-sidebar">
        <div class="sidebar-label">// Other Workshops</div>
        <nav class="sidebar-nav">
          <a href="/en/workshops/stunt/" class="sidebar-link">Stunt Workshop</a>
          <a href="/en/workshops/youth-circus/" class="sidebar-link">Youth Circus Workshop</a>
        </nav>
        <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
          <div class="sidebar-label">// Booking</div>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 13px; color: var(--gray); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 16px;">Book a workshop or request an offer — Ilian responds personally.</p>
          <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn-primary" style="display: block; text-align: center;">Get in Touch</a>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: 32px;">
          <div class="sidebar-label">// Skills</div>
          <p style="font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 13px; color: var(--gray); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 16px;">See Ilian's full fencing and combat skills.</p>
          <a href="/en/skills/" class="btn-outline-orange" style="display: block; text-align: center; padding: 12px;">View Skills</a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>

</Layout>

<style>
.page-hero { min-height: 40vh; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: flex-end; padding: 80px var(--page-pad) 56px; position: relative; background: linear-gradient(175deg, #0e0e0e 0%, #1c0c04 55%, #0e0e0e 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.page-hero-content { position: relative; z-index: 2; }
.page-hero-title { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(40px, 6vw, 80px); font-weight: bold; line-height: 0.95; letter-spacing: -2px; color: var(--white); margin-bottom: 20px; }
.page-hero-sub { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gray); }
.article-section { padding: var(--section-pad) var(--page-pad); background: var(--black); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
.article-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: start; }
.article-intro { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 20px; color: var(--white); line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 40px; padding-bottom: 40px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.article-h2 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 24px; color: var(--white); font-weight: bold; margin: 40px 0 16px; }
.article-body p { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 16px; color: var(--gray); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 16px; }
.article-list { margin: 16px 0 16px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
.article-list li { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 15px; color: var(--gray); padding-left: 20px; position: relative; }
.article-list li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 9px; width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--orange); }
.article-list li strong { color: var(--white); }
.article-callout { background: var(--card); border-left: 3px solid var(--orange); padding: 28px 24px; margin-top: 48px; }
.article-callout p { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 15px; color: var(--gray); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px; }
.article-sidebar { position: sticky; top: 88px; }
.sidebar-label { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--orange); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 16px; }
.sidebar-nav { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px; background: var(--border); }
.sidebar-link { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 14px; color: var(--gray); padding: 14px 16px; background: var(--card); display: block; transition: color 0.2s, background 0.2s; }
.sidebar-link:hover { color: var(--white); background: var(--black); }
</style>
